Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: shawk
Upstream-Contact: Yuuki TSUBOUCHI <yuki.tsubo@gmail.com>
Source: https://github.com/yuuki/shawk
Comment: /usr/bin/shawk embeds the compiled eBPF programs
 (internal/tracer/bpf_bpfel.o, see its paragraph). It also statically links
 the Go standard library and third-party Go modules, which are not part of
 this source and are under their own licenses (BSD-3-Clause, MIT,
 Apache-2.0 and others); their texts are in
 /usr/share/doc/shawk/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES. See also
 /usr/share/doc/shawk/NOTICE.

Files: *
Copyright: 2019-2026 Yuuki Tsubouchi
License: Apache-2.0

Files: internal/tracer/bpf_bpfel.o
Copyright: 2026 Yuuki Tsubouchi
 The libbpf authors (https://github.com/libbpf/libbpf)
 The Linux kernel authors
License: GPL-2 or BSD-2-clause
Comment: The eBPF object embedded in /usr/bin/shawk, compiled from the eBPF
 programs with the libbpf headers and the kernel types of vmlinux.h (see
 their paragraphs); it carries BTF descriptions of the kernel types the
 programs use, for CO-RE relocations.

Files: internal/tracer/bpf/shawk.bpf.c
 internal/tracer/bpf/shawk.h
Copyright: 2026 Yuuki Tsubouchi
License: GPL-2 or BSD-2-clause
Comment: The eBPF programs, which are loaded into the Linux kernel. The
 kernel only accepts programs that declare a GPL-compatible license when
 they use GPL-only helpers, so the programs declare "Dual BSD/GPL". The
 BSD-2-Clause option allows the compiled object to be distributed together
 with the Apache-2.0 code.

Files: internal/tracer/bpf/include/bpf_helpers.h
 internal/tracer/bpf/include/bpf_helper_defs.h
 internal/tracer/bpf/include/bpf_core_read.h
 internal/tracer/bpf/include/bpf_tracing.h
 internal/tracer/bpf/include/bpf_endian.h
Copyright: The libbpf authors (https://github.com/libbpf/libbpf)
License: LGPL-2.1 or BSD-2-clause
Comment: Copied from libbpf; shawk uses them under BSD-2-Clause.

Files: internal/tracer/bpf/include/vmlinux.h
Copyright: The Linux kernel authors
License: GPL-2
Comment: Generated by bpftool from the BTF type information of the Linux
 kernel (scripts/gen-vmlinux.sh). It contains type definitions; the
 compiled object carries BTF descriptions of the types the programs use,
 for CO-RE relocations.

